:0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.5 stable and 6efa557e\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.stable - Debian GNU/Linux 13 (trixie) 13 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1080 Ti (nvidia) - AMD Ryzen 5 3600X 6-Core Processor (12 threads) - 62.72 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\na very slight mismatch in error reporting when a superclass function is called and an error is printed (in the vm) it reports the function \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nrun the mrp.\n\ntheres nothing wrong in the stack trace tab, but in the errors tab:\n<img width=\"700\" height=\"134\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/40d5a776-25b7-412f-915e-8ad055eab7a2\" />\n\nit should say `A.fa` not `B.fa`\n\nand in the console when running without editor:\n<img width=\"716\" height=\"94\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3cb2f4a3-49fc-4687-91ad-94adb3860da0\" />\n\n`B.fa` does not exist and is not in `res://A.gd`\nit should be `at: A.fa (res://A.gd:5)`\nits strange that the file is correct, reading the code it looks like whoever wrote it meant `p_instance.get_script()->path` instead of `get_script()->path`, and both branches end up being  basically the same\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nmrp: [bug-wrong-source-file.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22385739/bug-wrong-source-file.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/us